(from Mark Moll)
Another odd feature/bug: if author names have accents, you need to 
surround the author field with curly braces; you can't use double 
quotes:

@Article{mendez+2003:asses-blind-predic-protein,
  author =       {Ra{\'u}l M{\'e}ndez and Rapha{\"e}l Leplae and Leonardo De
                  Maria and Shoshana J. Wodak},
  title =        "Assessment of Blind Predictions of Protein-Protein
                  Interactions: Current Status of Docking Methods",
  journal =      PSFG,
  year =         2003,
  volume =       52,
  pages =        "51--67",
  keywords =     "CAPRI, structure predictions, residue-residue contacts 
and
                  interface residues"
}

