D 1.      Add the possibility to adjoin a URL to each co-author
        (i.e. co-authors appear as links; the URLs can be define in
        the .conf file).

D 2.      Add a new bib2html_other_info bibitem category, where the user
        can write raw html code that will appear as _Additional
        Information: bla bla_ after the paper basic details are
        given. This is important for adding clarifications on papers
        or noting conference/journal duplications. Another option that
        it provides is to add links to demos, code or other sites
        relevant to the paper (this is why it would be good to allow
        writing the content in html or XML).

D 3.      In the download section add a link to the bibtex item when the
        user is not interested in the detailed pages (in which case
        this link is essential).

