DONE
If there is an accent in the last 
name of a first author, then the sort_author page doesn't display the 
accent correctly in the links at the top and at the header. Bib2html 
produces html like this:

         <h3><a 
name="Fern&amp;aacute;ndez-Recio"></a>Fern&amp;aacute;ndez-Recio
         </h3>
         <p class="citation">Juan Fern&aacute;ndez-Recio, Maxim Totrov, 
and Ruben                  Abagyan. Soft Protein-Protein Docking in 
Internal Coordinates.
            <i>Protein Science</i>, 11:280&ndash;291, 2002.<br><a 
href="b2hd-fernandez-recio2002soft-protein-protein-dockin.html">

So in the citation the accent is displayed correctly, but in the h3 
header it's not. Here's the complete bibtex entry, in case you want to 
try it yourself:

@Article{fernandez-recio+2002:soft-protein-protein-dockin,
  author =       "Juan Fern{\'a}ndez-Recio and Maxim Totrov and Ruben
                  Abagyan",
  title =        "Soft Protein-Protein Docking in Internal Coordinates",
  journal =      "Protein Science",
  year =         2002,
  volume =       11,
  pages =        "280--291",
  keywords =     "protein-protein docking, global energy optimization, grid
                  potentials, internal coordinate mechanics, biased
                  probability Monte Carlo, rigid docking with side-chain
                  refinement"
}

